  "description": "RUGQIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H98 Ce4 O15. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.570-4.377 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.04-153.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce4(μ4-O)(μ3-OPri)2(μ-OPri)4(OPri)8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
